    <string name="whats_new_title">Q25 Toolbox v3.1</string>
    <string name="whats_new_ok">Got it</string>
    <string name="whats_new_headline">Three additions ported from Key2 Toolbox: an ad blocker, backup/restore, and a wider telemetry block.</string>
    <string name="whats_new_body">AdBlock (Network tab) is a systemless hosts blocker — it installs a root-manager module and needs one reboot to activate, then edits are live.\n\nBackup and Restore (Settings tab) exports the selected modules\' settings to a JSON file and restores by merge.\n\nThe Telemetry block now also covers Firebase / Google Analytics and Performance Monitoring, re-scans every 10 minutes instead of 30, and reacts to app installs.\n\nThe Recents grid still needs an Xposed framework (LSPosed / Vector), unchanged since v3.0.</string>
    <string name="whats_new_matrix_title">Which version do I want?</string>
    <string name="whats_new_matrix">v3.0+  :  any stock-based Q25 ROM, with LSPosed / Vector\n2.1.1  :  BenOS beta3, no Xposed framework\n2.0.5  :  BenOS pre-beta3a / older stock</string>
    <string name="recents_intro">Makes Recents/Overview show two rows of smaller task cards, tablet-style, instead of the stock single row. It runs entirely through an LSPosed hook inside the launcher; this screen only stores the setting and restarts the launcher.</string>
    <string name="recents_section_lsposed">LSPosed needed</string>
    <string name="recents_xposed_ok">LSPosed module active.</string>
    <string name="recents_xposed_missing">LSPosed module not active.</string>
    <string name="recents_xposed_hint">Open your Xposed manager (LSPosed / Vector), enable \"Q25 Toolbox\", tick the launcher (com.android.launcher3) and this app in its scope, then force-stop the launcher. Requires an Xposed framework on KernelSU / APatch / Magisk.</string>
    <string name="recents_layout_title">Overview layout</string>
    <string name="recents_layout_desc">Grid forces the launcher\'s tablet two-row layout for Recents (the home screen and hotseat may shift slightly, since they share the layout profile). Masonry is Grid with staggered tile heights and square corners.</string>
